---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
---
<Guide
  title="Barre Class Planner for Instructors"
  description="Plan barre classes as a Flow, segment by segment, from a 280+ movement library. Built for instructors, not a workout app for students."
  kicker="Barre"
  heading="A barre class planner for instructors"
  crumb="Barre class planner"
>
  <div class="stack">
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>A class is a Flow.</h2>
      <p>We plan a barre class the same way we plan sculpt: Movements sit in Segments, and Segments build a Flow. One Segment is about one song. Organise Flows in folders, rearrange them, and add the notes you want to see while you teach.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>A library you can teach from.</h2>
      <p>The library holds 280+ sculpt, barre and Pilates movements, sorted by body part, plus movements you add yourself. Share a Flow with another teacher as a .sculptflow file. Movements you created travel with it. Catalogue movements they already have are not sent again.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card glass">
      <h2>Check the load, then cue the beat.</h2>
      <p>The intensity chart scores the Flow across core, glutes, legs, arms, shoulders, back and chest, and flags when one area is carrying the class. Cue Coach listens to the music in the room and shows a live BPM pulse. Apple Watch shows the current segment, the movements in it, a timer, notes and what comes next.</p>
    </article>
    <p>Sculpt Cues is for instructors planning group classes. It is not a workout app for students.</p>
  </div>
</Guide>
